## Session 33 summary — diagnosis substantially advanced (RULE 4, instrumented)

**PROVEN ROOT (this session, unambiguous):** the failure is **block double-OWNERSHIP** — an inode cluster gets overwritten by file data. `xfs_inode_buf_verify` EFSCORRUPTED at inode cluster block 0xc40/0xcc0; the buffer holds **random urandom file data** (no "IN" magic); `P26-IGET-FAIL inum=3136`/`3264` == those block numbers == the exact `.md5` files that fail `stat`. The dir-extent-map and leaf faces I chased early are **downstream** of this.

**Refuted / ruled out this session:**
- sess32's intra-dir double-alloc framing (P32B = 0).
- The "inode extent-map revert" I first chased — at the verify-phase miss, in-core == on-disk (nx=3/8192). My `P33-DIRGROW-REVERT-SKIP` reload guard fires **0× (no-op)**.
- My size/nx-shrink detectors and per-alloc disk probe were either no-ops or **timed out the test** (RULE 0) — reverted.

**Connected to prior work (sess30/sess55):** this is their FACE C / M2 "stale extent-map mis-write," NOT intra-node allocator double-alloc. Cross-node allocator double-alloc (M1) is *not* fully excluded but is now **disfavored**: `chk_mxfs` on a corrupted device shows **all AG btrees internally consistent** (no btree-level double-alloc).

**NEW concrete lead — `chk_mxfs` found durable superblock-counter incoherence:** `ifree=0` (vs 1616 free inodes in the inobt!), `icount` and `fdblocks` also mismatched vs the AG btrees. This is a **cross-node SB-summary-counter coherency bug** — a node allocating with `ifree=0`/wrong free-counts makes bad allocation decisions, a plausible contributing root that's more tractable than the per-buffer dir-coherency patches.

**Audited & found correct:** AG read-side coherency (TCP bumps `pag_dlm_meta_gen` every acquire → bnobt re-read) and release-side drain (`drain_meta_buffers` covers bnobt/cntbt/inobt + flush).

**Infra added (RULE 3):** `tests/reset2.sh` — virsh-reboots both VMs to clear the recurring D-state unmount wedge; **run it before every run**.

**Key lessons saved to memory:** dmesg ring-buffer **wraps** during 24-round runs → use `pr_warn_ratelimited`, not one-shot caps; extreme run-to-run **variance** (every run a different face) → run 3-5× before concluding.

**Next session (documented in 4 memories, head: `sess33-NEXT-action-plan-...` and `sess33-chkmxfs-SB-counter-incoherence-new-lead`):** (1) probe SB counter coherence at alloc-time / confirm the SB drift exists without corruption; (2) consider the structural fix — force per-node AG affinity for shared-dir file allocations to kill the cross-node AG contention; (3) `chk_mxfs`-after-corruption is the zero-cost decisive on-disk test.

